Package: blink
Title: Mean-Field (ODE) Twin of the 'malariasimulation' Malaria Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
  person("Peter", "Winskill", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "p.winskill@imperial.ac.uk"))
Description: Provides a fast, deterministic mean-field (ordinary differential
  equation) counterpart to the 'malariasimulation' individual-based model of
  Plasmodium falciparum malaria. The human population is structured by age and
  biting heterogeneity with the full acquired- and maternal-immunity model,
  coupled to a compartmental larval-and-adult mosquito model and driven by the
  same intervention modules: clinical treatment and antimalarial resistance,
  bed nets and indoor residual spraying, chemoprevention (MDA, SMC, PMC),
  pre-erythrocytic and transmission-blocking vaccines, seasonality, and custom
  demography. It accepts an unmodified 'malariasimulation' parameter list, is
  seeded at and validated against the 'malariaEquilibrium' fixed point, and
  returns 'malariasimulation'-style outputs that feed directly into 'postie'.
  Built on the 'odin2' and 'dust2' stack, a single multi-decade run completes in
  seconds, independent of population size.
